{
  "id": "graph-valid-tree",
  "questionId": "graph-valid-tree",
  "slug": "graph-valid-tree",
  "title": "Graph Valid Tree",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Union find",
  "patterns": [
    "union find",
    "cycle detection"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "a valid tree needs exactly two things: no cycles, and full connectivity - can you check both with one pass over the edges?",
    "a graph with n nodes and edges.length != n - 1 can never be a valid tree - check that first as a cheap short-circuit",
    "process edges one by one with union-find: if two endpoints are already in the same component before you union them, adding this edge creates a cycle",
    "if you get through every edge without finding a cycle, and the edge count already equals n - 1, the graph must be connected too"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to check the edge count equals n - 1 first, or relying on it alone without checking for cycles",
    "not detecting a cycle when two endpoints of an edge already share a root before unioning them",
    "treating a single node with zero edges as invalid instead of trivially valid"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given `n` nodes labeled 0 to n-1 and a list of undirected edges,\nwhere each edge is a pair `[u, v]`.\n\n**Return true if these edges form a valid tree, meaning the graph is connected and contains no cycles, and false otherwise.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 2000",
      "0 <= edges.length <= 5000",
      "edges are undirected, no self loops or repeated edges"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single node with no edges (trivially a valid tree)",
      "exactly n-1 edges but the graph is still disconnected (a cycle plus an isolated node)",
      "more than n-1 edges (guaranteed to contain a cycle)",
      "checking edge count alone is not sufficient - a graph can have exactly n-1 edges, a cycle, and a disconnected piece at the same time"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
